Description: arch: riscv64: add missing Bytes import in UEFI loader
 The riscv64 uefi.rs calls read_exact_volatile_from() which is provided
 by the vm_memory::Bytes trait, but the trait is not imported.  The
 identical aarch64/uefi.rs already has the import.  Without it the build
 fails with:
 .
   error[E0599]: no method named `read_exact_volatile_from` found for
   reference `&M` in the current scope
 .
 This is a subset of the upstream commit which also widens cfg gates for
 Instant and UEFI flash error paths on riscv64; those are feature
 enablement changes and are left for the next upstream release.
Author: wangyf0611 <wangyufeng@iscas.ac.cn>
Origin: upstream, https://github.com/cloud-hypervisor/cloud-hypervisor/commit/1e18716fbdc01df4538bb1604f6019d95ed29da3
Bug: https://github.com/cloud-hypervisor/cloud-hypervisor/issues/6978
Applied-Upstream: commit:1e18716fbdc01df4538bb1604f6019d95ed29da3
Last-Update: 2026-07-01
---
--- a/arch/src/riscv64/uefi.rs
+++ b/arch/src/riscv64/uefi.rs
@@ -7,7 +7,7 @@
 use std::result;
 
 use thiserror::Error;
-use vm_memory::{GuestAddress, GuestMemory};
+use vm_memory::{Bytes, GuestAddress, GuestMemory};
 
 /// Errors thrown while loading UEFI binary
 #[derive(Debug, Error)]
